mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown documentation of the public backend API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# RzzPr2tg Ai — Backend API\n\nBackend for the RzzPr2tg Ai chat application. It runs chat completions through\nCaffeine Inference, persists per-user conversation history, stores per-user\nprofiles, and exposes the stored data to the Caffeine Data Intelligence agent\nthrough OQL.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nThe frontend authenticates with Internet Identity. Google, Microsoft, and\nemail/password sign-in are all Internet Identity flows; the canister only ever\nsees the resulting principal. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation\norigin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An\nagent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the\ncorrect per-app principal against that origin (for example\n`icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\nuser's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nThere is no registration step and no role gate on the chat or profile methods.\nA caller is identified by its principal alone:\n\n- **Anonymous callers** (`caller.isAnonymous()`) are treated as guests. They can\n  run chat completions, but nothing is persisted for them.\n- **Signed-in callers** (any non-anonymous principal) own their conversation\n  history and profile. Each caller only ever reads and writes its own data.\n- **Controllers** (the platform principal that installed the canister) are the\n  only callers that can read every user's rows through OQL.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `sendChatMessage(request : ChatRequest) : async ChatResponse`\n\nRuns one chat completion and, for signed-in callers, persists the exchange.\n\n- `request.messages` is the full ordered history the model should see, oldest\n  first. It must be non-empty; an empty list traps with\n  `Tidak ada pesan untuk dikirim`.\n- `request.conversationId` is `null` to start a new conversation, or an existing\n  conversation id to append to. A non-null id that does not belong to the caller\n  traps with `Percakapan tidak ditemukan`.\n- `request.systemPrompt` optionally prepends a system instruction to the model\n  context. It is not persisted.\n- Returns `{ conversationId; reply; message }`. For guests `conversationId` is\n  `0` and `message.id` is `0`, because nothing is stored.\n- If the inference service cannot be reached, the call traps with\n  `Gagal menghubungi layanan AI. Silakan coba lagi.`\n\n### `sendChatMessageStream(request : ChatRequest) : async ChatStreamResponse`\n\nRuns one chat completion and returns the assistant reply split into ordered\nchunks so the frontend can render it incrementally. It accepts the same\n`ChatRequest` as `sendChatMessage` and applies the same validation, persistence,\nand error behavior: signed-in callers get the exchange persisted exactly as\nbefore, guests stay unpersisted (`conversationId = 0`, `message.id = 0`).\n\n- Returns `{ conversationId; chunks; message }`. `chunks` is an ordered list of\n  `Text` fragments whose concatenation is exactly the full reply; `message` is\n  the persisted assistant message (or the transient guest message).\n- The chunks are produced by the backend in one update call, so the frontend\n  receives them together and appends them in order to animate the reply.\n- Traps are identical to `sendChatMessage` (`Tidak ada pesan untuk dikirim`,\n  `Percakapan tidak ditemukan`, `Gagal menghubungi layanan AI. Silakan coba lagi.`).\n\n### `listConversations() : async [ConversationSummary]`\n\nReturns the caller's conversation summaries, newest first by `updatedAt`.\nAnonymous callers receive `[]`.\n\n### `getConversation(id : ConversationId) : async ?Conversation`\n\nReturns one of the caller's conversations with all of its messages, or `null`\nwhen it does not exist or does not belong to the caller. Anonymous callers\nreceive `null`.\n\n### `deleteConversation(id : ConversationId) : async Bool`\n\nDeletes one of the caller's conversations. Returns `true` when it existed and\nwas removed, `false` otherwise. Anonymous callers receive `false`.\n\n### `getCallerUserProfile() : async ?UserProfile`\n\nReturns the caller's own profile, or `null` when none has been saved or the\ncaller is anonymous.\n\n### `saveCallerUserProfile(profile : UserProfile) : async ()`\n\nCreates or replaces the caller's own profile. Anonymous callers are ignored\n(no-op).\n\n### `getUserProfile(user : Principal) : async ?UserProfile`\n\nReturns a profile by principal, but only when the requested principal is the\ncaller itself, or when the caller is an admin. Anonymous callers and\nnon-admin callers requesting another principal receive `null`; no other\nprincipal's profile data is ever disclosed.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nReturns this document.\n\n## Types and encoding\n\n- `ConversationId`, `MessageId`, and `Timestamp` are `Nat`.\n- `Timestamp` is nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Int.abs(Time.now())`).\n- `MessageRole` is the variant `{ #user; #assistant }`.\n- `ChatMessage` is `{ id : MessageId; role : MessageRole; content : Text; createdAt : Timestamp }`.\n- `ConversationSummary` is `{ id; title; createdAt; updatedAt; messageCount }`.\n- `Conversation` is `{ id; title; createdAt; updatedAt; messages : [ChatMessage] }`.\n- `ChatStreamResponse` is `{ conversationId; chunks : [Text]; message : ChatMessage }`.\n- `UserProfile` is `{ displayName : Text; email : ?Text; photoUrl : ?Text }`.\n  `email` and `photoUrl` are optional and may be `null`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n`sendChatMessage` and `sendChatMessageStream` are single update calls that\nreturn only after the model reply has been produced and persisted. There is no\njob id and nothing to poll: the returned `ChatResponse` / `ChatStreamResponse`\nis the final result. `sendChatMessageStream` returns the reply as ordered\nchunks in that same single response; the frontend appends them in order. A new conversation is created\nimplicitly on the first message when `conversationId` is `null`; its title is\nderived from the first user message (truncated to 60 characters, or\n`Percakapan Baru` when the message is blank).\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n`sendChatMessage` and `sendChatMessageStream` are **not idempotent**. Retrying\nthe same request appends the user turns and the assistant reply again, and a\nretry with `conversationId = null` creates a second conversation. After a timeout, re-read\n`listConversations` before retrying, and pass the existing `conversationId` to\navoid duplicating history.\n\n`deleteConversation` is idempotent in effect: deleting an already-deleted id\nreturns `false` and changes nothing. `saveCallerUserProfile` is a full replace,\nso repeating it with the same payload is safe.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- Traps are returned to the frontend as opaque rejects; the messages above are\n  the human-readable text the frontend surfaces.\n- Guest sessions are temporary by design: guest chats are never written to\n  stable storage and are lost when the session ends.\n- Conversation history is stored per principal. A caller that signs in with a\n  different Internet Identity derivation origin is a different principal and\n  will not see the first principal's history.\n\n## OQL (Data Intelligence)\n\nThe canister exposes two query endpoints through the OQL `Expose` mixin:\n\n- `schema()` — the discoverable schema of the exposed entities.\n- `execute(queryJson)` — runs a JSON query against them.\n\nTwo entities are exposed, both scoped per user and readable by controllers:\n\n- `conversation` — columns `owner`, `id`, `title`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`,\n  `messageCount`. Primary key `id`.\n- `profile` — columns `owner`, `displayName`, `email`, `photoUrl`. Primary key\n  `owner`.\n\nA signed-in caller querying these entities sees only its own rows; the platform\ncontroller sees all rows. Anonymous callers are denied.\n";
  };
};
